{"id":"n2-054","title":"～からといって","romaji":"〜kara to itte","jlptLevel":2,"shortExplanation":"Expresses 'just because...doesn't mean' or 'even though...not necessarily'.","longExplanation":"The ～からといって grammar point is used to convey that even though something is true, it does not necessarily mean a certain result will occur. It can be translated as 'just because...doesn't mean' or 'even though...not necessarily.'","formation":"Verb-casual + からといって, い-Adjective + からといって, な-Adjective + だからといって, Noun + だからといって","examples":[{"jp":"雨が降ったからといって、試合が中止になるわけではありません。","romaji":"Ame ga futta kara to itte, shiai ga chuushi ni naru wake de wa arimasen.","en":"Just because it rained doesn't mean the game will be canceled.","words":[{"surface":"雨","vocabId":"1171900","reading":"あめ"},{"surface":"が","vocabId":null},{"surface":"降ったから","vocabId":"1282790","reading":"ふったから","baseForm":"降る"},{"surface":"と","vocabId":null},{"surface":"いっ","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"いう"},{"surface":"て","vocabId":null},{"surface":"、","vocabId":null},{"surface":"試合","vocabId":"1312420","reading":"しあい"},{"surface":"が","vocabId":null},{"surface":"中止","vocabId":"1424410","reading":"ちゅうし"},{"surface":"に","vocabId":null},{"surface":"なる","vocabId":null},{"surface":"わけ","vocabId":null},{"surface":"で","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"だ"},{"surface":"は","vocabId":null},{"surface":"あり","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"ある"},{"surface":"ませ","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"ます"},{"surface":"ん","vocabId":null},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[2,3,4,5]},{"jp":"彼が有名だからといって、彼の意見がいつも正しいわけではない。","romaji":"Kare ga yuumei da kara to itte, kare no iken ga itsumo tadashii wake de wa nai.","en":"Just because he is famous doesn't mean his opinions are always correct.","words":[{"surface":"彼","vocabId":"1483070","reading":"かれ"},{"surface":"が","vocabId":null},{"surface":"有名","vocabId":"1541620","reading":"ゆうめい"},{"surface":"だ","vocabId":null},{"surface":"から","vocabId":null},{"surface":"と","vocabId":null},{"surface":"いっ","vocabId":n